        #revision
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Let
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_1.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a group or a discrete groupoid. Recall that an associative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semigroup"} semigroup
            (if unital then monoid) in the category of abelian groups and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantale"} quantale
            a semigroup in the category of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sup-lattice"} sup-lattice
          %p
            While
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+algebra"} group(oid) ring
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}G
            is the free abelian group with basis
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            (resp.
            = succeed ")" do
              %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mor(G)
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and the convolution product making it a quantale.
          %h2#constructiondefinition Construction-definition
          %p
            The free sup-lattice on a set
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the power set
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(X)
            (set of subsets of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Vee
            (infinite join) and meet
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∧
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge
            respectively; or equivalently the set
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mn 2
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^X
            of boolean functions on
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = Mor(C)
            is a morphism set of a category (special cases: semigroup, group, groupoid) then
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(Mor(C))
            has the multiplication
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mi B
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi a
                  %mi b
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi and
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi b
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi compose
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A B = \{ a b \,|\, a\in A, b\in B, a\,\,\, and\,\,\, b\,\,\, compose \}
          %p
            or, in terms of functions (the characteristic function of the subsets of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %mi Mor
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g\in 2^{Mor(C)}
            %strong convolution product
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo *
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %mi a
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (f \ast g)(c) = \Vee \{ f(a)\wedge f(b)\,|\, c = a b \}
          %p
            This way,
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_19.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mn 2
                    %mrow
                      %mi Mor
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^{Mor(C)}
            becomes a quantale denoted simply
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_20.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^C
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_21.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(Mor(C))
            is the set of units
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_22.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ob(C) = C_0
            of the quantale which is canonically identified with a subset of
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_23.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mor(C)
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_24.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
          %p
            If
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_25.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = G
            is a groupoid, then there is an additional involution
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_26.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⋆
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \star
            on
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_27.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(Mor(G))
            where
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_28.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⋆
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi g
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X^\star = \{ g^{-1} \,|\, g\in X \}
          %p
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_29.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \subset Mor(G)
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_30.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^G
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_11e2f350dd1d41db9342dd91963e92b8ff6b451b_31.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mn 2
                    %mrow
                      %mi Mor
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f^*(g) = f(g^{-1}), \,\,\,\,f\in 2^{Mor(G)}, g\in G.
          %p This groupoid quantale is therefore an involutive unital quantale.
